      "side": 1,
      "message": "**DRY Principle in `filecontrol.cc`:** `getBinarySize` and `getBinary` share near-identical logic for opening the file, validating the stream, and calculating the stream position. You can significantly clean this up by having `getBinary` call `getBinarySize` first, rather than duplicating the file I/O boilerplate.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 11,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 62,
        "endChar": 1
      },
      "revId": "53f5e96a6fdf9b8ef17bf51d73af71f1bcc80a46",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "08196152_a7997ae3",
        "filename": "util/elan/filecontrol.cc",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 62,
      "author": {
        "id": 1314845
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-04-27T16:27:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Here is an example generated by Gemini. Review the code to make sure it is correct before using it:\n\n----\n\n```\n// Copyright 2026 The ChromiumOS Authors\n// Use of this source code is governed by a BSD-style license that can be\n// found in the LICENSE file.\n\n#include \"filecontrol.h\"\n\n#include \u003cformat\u003e\n#include \u003cfstream\u003e\n#include \u003ciostream\u003e\n\nstd::optional\u003csize_t\u003e getBinarySize(const std::string \u0026filePath)\n{\n\tstd::ifstream binFile(filePath, std::ios::binary | std::ios::ate);\n\n\tif (!binFile) {\n\t\tstd::cout \u003c\u003c std::format(\"[IAP] {} - open file fail ({})\\n\",\n\t\t\t\t\t __func__, filePath);\n\t\treturn std::nullopt;\n\t}\n\n\tstd::streampos pos \u003d binFile.tellg();\n\tif (pos \u003d\u003d std::streampos(-1) || pos \u003d\u003d 0) {\n\t\tstd::cout \u003c\u003c std::format(\"[IAP] {} - file size is 0 or invalid\\n\", \n\t\t\t\t\t __func__);\n\t\treturn std::nullopt;\n\t}\n\n\treturn static_cast\u003csize_t\u003e(pos);\n}\n\nstd::optional\u003cstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e\u003e getBinary(const std::string \u0026filePath)\n{\n\tauto sizeOpt \u003d getBinarySize(filePath);\n\tif (!sizeOpt) {\n\t\treturn std::nullopt;\n\t}\n\n\tsize_t size \u003d *sizeOpt;\n\n\tstd::ifstream binFile(filePath, std::ios::binary);\n\tif (!binFile) {\n\t\tstd::cout \u003c\u003c std::format(\"[IAP] {} - open file fail ({})\\n\",\n\t\t\t\t\t __func__, filePath);\n\t\treturn std::nullopt;\n\t}\n\n\tstd::vector\u003cuint8_t\u003e buffer(size);\n\tif (binFile.read(reinterpret_cast\u003cchar *\u003e(buffer.data()), size)) {\n\t\treturn buffer;\n\t}\n\n\tstd::cout \u003c\u003c std::format(\"[IAP] {} - read file data fail\\n\", __func__);\n\treturn std::nullopt;\n}\n```",
      "parentUuid": "7b6f000c_4150f7d0",
