      "side": 1,
      "message": "**Variable Shadowing:** In `iapcontrol.cc` inside `runIapProcess`, the `result` variable is declared at the top level (`int result \u003d 0;`). Further down, it is shadowed multiple times:\n\n```c\nif (auto result \u003d getChecksum(rom)) {\n```\n\n  While valid C++, this can make debugging confusing. \n  \nIt looks like this `result` is never used in the function, so remove this variable and make the function `return 0` at the end.",
